 "result_text": "Equation fields now use Knack's own formatted value for `.formatted`, so the day-based number from your example should show up instead of the raw seconds. I haven't run it against real Knack data, and I didn't run any tests. The only check was that `import knackpy` still works.\n\n- **`knackpy/models.py`:** I added `\"equation\": {\"use_knack_format\": True}` to `FIELD_SETTINGS`. This is the same setting `timer` and `name` fields use. `.raw` still holds the `_raw` value.\n- **`knackpy/fields.py`:** `Field._format` used to check whether the Knack formatted value was truthy. That would have sent an equation result of `0` back to the raw value. It now checks `is not None`.\n\nThe edit to `knackpy/models.py` shows up as changed on disk after I made it. I didn't read the file again, so I haven't confirmed the equation line is still in the current version.",
